{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfXVu7Xbkd9v4xvNxxiyk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noticing that for B, review-passed responses fail verification more often as length exceeds roughly 830 tokens. I'm breaking the data into finer bins to check this pattern more carefully before writing up the findings, and the failure rate does seem to climb in the higher length ranges while shorter responses pass consistently.\n\nRefining the estimate this way gives about 0.762 compared to 0.7545 with coarser bins, close enough to be reassuring — a logistic fit would be another useful cross-check. Separately, I'm flagging that the Q3 verdict is statistically shaky given how small the effect size is relative to its standard error, worth calling out explicitly. I want to run a bootstrap on the sign probability and try a quick logistic fit before finalizing the report.\n\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19611,"cache_read_input_tokens":19990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19611,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4561f34-0830-4521-abc3-8f6651b2757a","uuid":"dffb7f3c-56ed-43e1-84dd-369405805c46","timestamp":"2026-09-29T09:32:25.845Z"}
